Irish gambling study puts account controls and marketing in focus

An ESRI study published on 4 November for Ireland’s regulator GRAI found that 54% of people who opened an online gambling account went on to open another. One in seven respondents said their latest online session followed an email, app notification or gambling ad. GRAI highlighted account controls, marketing standards and self-exclusion as priorities. The study itself introduces no new rules.

